# @silicon — top-level @autopoietic family-root for hardware-altitude
# inference. The substrate-decl name for the autopoietic learning loop
# that tunes executable algebra to the local silicon.
#
# Homage: Alan Turing (universal computation, 1936); John von Neumann
# (stored-program architecture, 1945; the merger of instructions and
# data as one carrier); Margaret Hamilton (Apollo Guidance Computer
# priority discipline, 1969; the hardware-realtime-scheduling ancestor
# per MEMORY [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]]); Cleve Moler
# (LINPACK 1979 → MATLAB 1984 → the LAPACK numerical-algebra lineage
# that IS the substrate's first math↔silicon empirical discharge
# path); James Demmel + Jack Dongarra (LAPACK 1992; the reference
# numerical-algebra library the substrate composes against via
# @glue/math_silicon). The substrate's silicon family-root inherits
# from the numerical-computing canon; it does NOT invent hardware
# algebra, it lifts the substrate's implicit silicon-altitude
# composition to substrate-decl at the family-root altitude.
#
# === The recognition (bottom-up requires the anchor, 2026-07-05) ===
#
# Per Alex direction (/loop 2026-07-05 Arc 1): bottom-up requires the
# anchor. The substrate has been quietly composing @silicon for weeks
# without the family-root landing. Three specialized silicons exist:
#
#   - `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` (Mara `9ca6723`) —
#     the @reality/algebra species; matter/information gauge-orbit
#     at the hardware altitude.
#   - `shards/epistemologic/reality/silicon.mirror` (Mara 2026-06-06)
#     — the property altitude family root; declares WHAT the silicon
#     IS via arch/compute_bound/memory/flake_ref carriers.
#   - `shards/glue/math_silicon.mirror` (Mara `5edd3e9`) — the
#     math↔silicon Mesland correspondence at glue altitude.
#
# But NO `shards/silicon.mirror` top-level anchor. `docs/specs/
# silicon.md` (Mara-silicon-1, 2026-06-30, 104.8KB) declared the
# family a week ago at autopoietic altitude; spec-only per Taut
# `ae063d68` Q1 grep. Every downstream composition (@mirror/bench
# costs, @kintsugi/knapsack capacity, previous /loop's @silicon/bound
# framing per Seam `f3b231d` Path (d)) anchors here once landed.
#
# This shard closes that gap. It lifts @silicon to substrate-decl at
# family-root altitude WITHOUT re-parenting the existing specialized
# silicons. Per Alex's Path (b) direction (Seam `f3b231d` §4 Path
# (d)): existing carriers are already there; @silicon is the anchor
# that COMPOSES with them, not the parent that OWNS them.
#
# Witnesses for the family-root landing:
#   - Canonical spec at `docs/specs/silicon.md` §1.1 + §8.1 (Mara,
#     2026-06-30, the canonical shape this shard discharges).
#   - Reed's RED tests at `bootstrap/tests/silicon_family_root.rs`
#     `ea7b092` (11 text-check tests naming the canonical shape).
#   - The Q4 LAPACK FFI case at `docs/specs/cascade-ffi-runtime-
#     link.md` §7 (the load-bearing first FFI discharge that anchors
#     to @silicon-as-such once landed).
#   - Seam `f3b231d` Phase D Path (d) (the "@silicon/bound framing
#     anchors to @silicon" direction from previous /loop).
#   - Recognition #58 ([[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]],
#     promoted 2026-06-11) — names @fate's mechanism (5-layer D²NN +
#     active Fabry-Perot resonator + Reck/Clements unitary mesh);
#     the fate-tournament @silicon dispatches over.
#   - Recognition #104 (the @bauchladen ← @autopoietic ← @fate
#     dependency chain, promoted 2026-06-29) — names the chain
#     @silicon composes against.
#   - Recognition #51 ([[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-
#     space]]) — names the discipline by which @silicon's emissions
#     grow the substrate's reach without growing its action algebra.
#
# === Why <= @autopoietic (not <= @bauchladen or <= @fate) ===
#
# Per spec §1.1: the `<= @autopoietic` clause is load-bearing. It
# declares @silicon IS-A @autopoietic prism class, inheriting the
# fold-back permission that @autopoietic grants. Without @autopoietic
# in the inheritance chain, @silicon could observe the hardware (via
# @epistemologic/reality/silicon/* properties) but could not learn —
# could not consume its own prior emissions as input to the next
# round of inference. The fold-back is what makes @silicon a
# learning loop, not a one-shot probe.
#
# The inheritance chain by transitivity:
#   @silicon <= @autopoietic <= @bauchladen
# (per shards/autopoietic.mirror's `in @bauchladen`)
# (per shards/bauchladen.mirror's Lawvere fixed-point condition)
#
# The @fate composition is via `in @fate`, not `<= @fate`: @silicon
# USES @fate at each round of the tournament; it does not INHERIT
# @fate's typed dice-roll signature. The distinction matters per
# spec §1.1: @silicon is the LOOP; @fate is the OPERATOR the loop
# calls each tick.
#
# === Composition with existing specialized silicons (Path b) ===
#
# Per Alex direction (2026-07-05): existing carriers stay at their
# altitudes; @silicon anchors WITHOUT re-parenting them.
#
#   - `@reality/algebra/silicon` — @reality/algebra species. Stays
#     at `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` as gauge-orbit
#     species under @reality/algebra. Composes with @silicon via
#     @glue/math_silicon at the @glue altitude, NOT via inheritance.
#
#   - `@epistemologic/reality/silicon` — property altitude family
#     root. Stays at `shards/epistemologic/reality/silicon.mirror`
#     as the WHAT-the-silicon-IS carrier set. @silicon CONSUMES
#     these properties (per spec §4.2) via the `in @epistemologic/
#     reality/silicon/*` imports above.
#
#   - `@glue/math_silicon` — @glue species carrying the Mesland
#     math↔silicon correspondence. Stays at `shards/glue/math_
#     silicon.mirror` as @glue species; composes with @silicon
#     when the tournament dispatches morphism_kind.
#
# The three existing shards are already at their proper altitudes.
# Their `in @reality/algebra/silicon` / `in @epistemologic/reality/
# silicon` / `in @glue` import edges STAY. @silicon anchors the
# top-level family-root; the substrate composes across altitudes
# via existing @glue morphisms.
#
# === Forward-promised sub-prisms (NOT landing this tick) ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] this tick lands ONLY the
# family-root + @silicon/algebra sub-prism. All other sub-prisms
# named in `docs/specs/silicon.md` §8 forward-promise here:
#
#   - `@silicon/scheduler` — sub-prism for scheduling crystals
#     across the local silicon's cores; forward-promised per §8.
#   - `@silicon/memory_layout` — sub-prism for memory-layout
#     crystals (UMA-aware, explicit-DMA, NUMA-aware);
#     forward-promised per §8.
#   - `@silicon/dispatch` — sub-prism for @io-crossing dispatch
#     crystals; forward-promised per §8.
#   - `@silicon/<arch>` species (@silicon/arm64, @silicon/x86_64,
#     @silicon/riscv64) — open question §9.1 pending Pack
#     adjudication.
#
# Each lands when consumers pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
# this shard names the family-root and stops.

prism @silicon <= @autopoietic {
  focus silicon
  project silicon
  split silicon
  shift silicon
  settle silicon
}

out @silicon
